    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d211">

                <pb facs="0241" n="229" sameAs="frus:frus1945v04/pg229"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">874.00/5–2645: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State
                        to the United States Representative in Bulgaria</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Barnes</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-05-26T19:00:00-04:00">May 26, 1945—7
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>148. You will of course not resist by force an attempt to take Dimitrov by force
                    but if he is removed from your house you should try with all earnestness to
                    obtain an assurance that he will be kept in safe custody until the US, UK and
                    Soviet Governments advise the Bulgarian authorities of the positions which they
                    individually or collectively wish to take in the circumstances. Did you receive
                    our 143 and 144 yesterday’s date and today’s message to Moscow repeated to
                        you?<anchor n="66" xml:id="d211-f1"/> (Sent to Sofia, repeated to London,
                    Moscow and Caserta.<anchor n="67" xml:id="d211-f2"/>)</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Grew</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
